From 090bd8da44b3086f033d258ccebc3439b49a9589 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:08:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x86: perfect operand-direction, prefix, and i686 encoding
 laws (GAS 2.47-probed)

VEX/EVEX + legacy x86/i686 assembler encoder completion, verified against
the GAS 2.47 oracles on both x86-64 and i686 (insndiff/asmdiff/encdiff
sweeps: x86-64 ENCDIFF 0 over the 268-line .s matrix, FALSEACC 0; i686
WRONG-class divergences 242 -> 102 -> clean on the covered classes).

x86-64:
- Honor the `.s` store/swap-direction suffix everywhere (ALU, all vector
  move families, x87, AES/SHA, PCLMUL, monitor-class): `.s` forces the
  store-form opcode and dst-in-reg operand order unconditionally, even
  when the swapped form is longer (GAS semantics). Fixes five wrong-byte
  classes; ALU `.s` is semantically live (03 ca != 01 d1), superseding the
  stale "GAS ignores .s for ALU" comment.
- vmovd/movd `.s` xmm<->xmm unlocks the previously rejected line and
  promotes to EVEX D6 (62 f1 7d 08 d6 e6 probed).
- uwrmsr/urdmsr: REX follows operand roles, not modrm position; F3
  precedes REX. monitor: first operand is an address hint; 67 iff the
  hint disagrees with the mode default.
- mov-to-segment, pushw, and pop direction laws aligned with GAS.

i686:
- Register-size inference for ALU/shift/imul/cmovcc/movx: byte forms are
  emitted when byte registers are operands (add %dl,%cl -> 00 d1, not the
  widened 01 d1), 16-bit operand sizes no longer silently widen to 32.
- Split cvtsd2si (rounding, 0x2D) from cvttsd2si (truncation, 0x2C);
  both previously emitted 0x2C.
- MMX no longer encodes as the SSE2-66 form; segment-register moves,
  prefix words (addr32/data16/rex), and monitor matrices match GAS.
- GOT immediate law: `mov $sym@GOTPC/%reg` carries the relocation with
  the correct addend; call/jmp direct addends follow GAS.
- Displacement union bounds fixed to [-2^(N-1), 2^N-1] (GAS-probed), so
  0x80000000-class displacements no longer misclassify.
- Branch size laws: 16-bit indirect calls, string-op addressing, and
  patch-pass addr16 awareness.

Tests: new exhaustive casefiles (suffix-s 138 lines, prefix-words x86-64
+ i686, i686 system + symgot) byte-locked against GAS 2.47 oracles; the
full asm-diff suite passes 1316/1316 x86-64 and the i686 suite with
FALSEACC 0; sweeps re-generated for both targets.
